;; this note used to cite target-continue's raw, undecoded :code/:event
;; (bare label references, :code L1/:event L65) and its own decoded-but-held
;; :exit together, since the camera-combiner offset-140 type, the
;; event-message-block param typing, and two unsupported inline sllv sites
;; all blocked in the same function. All three now resolve; see the wall
;; resolution table on target-continue's own defstate (logic-target.gc,
;; where the real :code/:event/:enter/:trans/:post are landed). :exit alone
;; is still held there (its own setting-control-method-17 call reads two
;; registers, a3/t0, with no recoverable retail value); its citation moved
;; with it rather than staying split across two files. The raw held block
;; that used to sit here is gone: it is superseded by the landed source, not
;; merely duplicated by it.
